<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19239" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gălī^laea</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γαλιλαία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the province of
				Galilee in northern Palestine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 14,
				15, § 70</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gălī^laeus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Galilee</i>, <i>Galilean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gălĭlaea per arva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sedul. 4, 188</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gălīlaeas repetat Salvator
					in oras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 3, 195</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Galilaei</span></b> , ōrum,
				m., <i>the inhabitants of Galilee</i>,
				<i>Galileans</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 12,
				54</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
